{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/51517-how-an-angel-dies-regina","id":51517,"title":"How An Angel Dies - Regina","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-17T03:58:15-08:00","id":51517,"title":"How An Angel Dies - Regina","content":"SPOILER WARNING<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> <br /> I'm puzzled about the purpose of the desire of breaking the phone implanted on Regina. It's stated that she felt this desire first when she witnessed Simon getting into the VW, and in her roleplaying hints we're told this action was implanted by the God-Machine. Then we find out the phone Regina is repeatedly breaking is the linchpin of an Infrastructure, and it's supposed to build power over time and then summon the Lambent but the circuit was broken due to Regina smashing it and thus preventing the Lambent to turn up until it's replaced or fixed (or that's my read).<br /> <br /> Now if I understood all that correctly, why would the God-Machine implant Regina with the urge to break the phone and thus sabotage its own occult matrix?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just a bit to showcase how the God-Machine acts in really contriving and seemingly illogical to us ways, but the whole thing doesn't even feel like it was for a purpose. Maybe this bit of the scenario is meant to be used as a foreshadowing for a Storyteller who wishes to take on it and develop around it, but it would be worth making it explicit.<br /> <br /> In any case, could anyone either explain to me the purpose or the reasoning of this as written, or did anyone come up with a good fix or alternate backstory for Regina's action?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2022-rancor","name":"Rancor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T08:22:09-08:00","id":51626,"title":"","content":"Reading it, the likeliest interpretation is that the God-Machine didn't intentionally implant that that idea in Regina's mind. It was the encounter that's directly responsible for it, not the God-Machine itself. Her sensibility to Machine-y stuff as a Stigmatic is what allows her to pick up the telephone linchpin as something she needs to destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-17T10:39:00-08:00","id":51700,"title":"","content":"Breaking the circuit keeps the portal open and allows the God-Machine to access the 1962 splinter more easily than the Space Needle Observation Deck fracture. Considering the implication that the '62 splinter may have been made <i>deliberately</i>, mechanisms are likely in place to allow Regina to continue to break that phone until some failsafe trips and it becomes more trouble than it's worth to allow the VW to remain a viable route for anybody. A giant demon-wolf razing the city is one of the sort of things things that necessitates those failsafes; remember that not being able to otherwise stop Marchosias from leaving the splinter (courtesy of Simon) is the reason the Lambent is being summoned to destroy the way out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}